<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Breaking news from AFRICA, Maghreb and Sub-Saharan Africa - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of events, politics and social issues across Africa, including North Africa (the Maghreb) and the Sahel, aided by our network of correspondents and experts across the continent.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/rss</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Kenya reports first-ever Ebola death</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:749c8df01a6458136cf7ce164083f90b8912bcd30532760d49a62f723a169dbc</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T21:28:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/kenya-reports-first-ever-ebola-death" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition, Kenya records its first Ebola death after a man travelled from the DRC via Uganda. Also, Comoros is tightening the rules on who can do business. In South Africa, concerns are growing that xenophobia and hostility toward foreign nationals could be driving African tourists away.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Kenya reports first-ever Ebola death after patient returns from DR Congo</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c858737a8c86af14c196513bfd8e032c4cf759b431cb84d7cb286a280ef78aac</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T15:41:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261006-kenya-reports-first-ever-ebola-death-after-patient-returns-from-dr-congo--ad7202bd54ed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261006-kenya-reports-first-ever-ebola-death-after-patient-returns-from-dr-congo" /><summary type="html">Kenya on Tuesday reported its first-ever Ebola death after a Kenyan national who had been living in the Democratic Republic of Congo (DR Congo) died after returning to the country. Kenya is the fourth country to record an Ebola case in the current outbreak, which was declared in eastern DR Congo in mid-May.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia again demands access to the Red Sea</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:59f6cc42a667c389ab59961de23032112ccd9e9ba68f3cff6a16bb10cafa9d43</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T20:28:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ethiopia-again-demands-access-to-the-red-sea--806dbf10a5ba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ethiopia-again-demands-access-to-the-red-sea" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition: Ethiopia's leader Abiy Ahmed secures another term in office, but his country is sliding back into conflict. Also, several major cities across Senegal are battered by torrential rains. Plus some of the migrants being deported from the US fear being sent to African countries criminalising homosexuality.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Rwandan genocide suspect 'hunter' Dafroza Gauthier dies at 72</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:06a75bd2eb354d7f928e0282b359eac105b94720ca38d8f52309d6154b5f2cf0</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T12:12:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261004-rwandan-genocide-hunter-dafroza-gauthier-dies-at-72--4acbb8946f0b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261004-rwandan-genocide-hunter-dafroza-gauthier-dies-at-72" /><summary type="html">For nearly 30 years, Dafroza Gauthier, along with her husband Alain, tracked down Rwandan refugees in France suspected of having participated in the Tutsi genocide. She died in Reims on Saturday after dedicating her life to bringing to justice those allegedly responsible for the 1994 massacre of more than 800,000 people.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopian federal forces control Tigray capital as regional rivals meet in Egypt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:69fd0f119879625a9d6ef591b3534faed1f5536d174f231fa50618427ae106df</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T10:22:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261004-ethiopian-federal-forces-control-tigray-capital-as-regional-rivals-meet-in-egypt--ec257ed5cbcd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261004-ethiopian-federal-forces-control-tigray-capital-as-regional-rivals-meet-in-egypt" /><summary type="html">Troops loyal to Ethiopia's federal government were patrolling the streets of Mekelle on Sunday, a day after the Tigray People's Liberation Front (TPLF) withdrew its forces from the northern city. The government advance came as Ethiopia's regional rivals including Eritrea and Sudan met in the Egyptian coastal city of El-Alamein, calling for regional disputes to be settled through "peaceful means".</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia's Tigray rebels abandon regional capital Mekelle as government forces enter city</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1db7a4072e5e2bc1563fbe48e54e23255e840fb0ba59f41818f798129e914738</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T07:58:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261003-ethiopia-s-tigray-rebels-abandon-regional-capital-of-mekelle-as-pro-government-forces-advan--a3cb00a5f7af.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261003-ethiopia-s-tigray-rebels-abandon-regional-capital-of-mekelle-as-pro-government-forces-advance" /><summary type="html">Ethiopian federal forces have entered the capital of the northern Tigray region and seized its airport, witnesses said Saturday, reversing a takeover by rebels from the Tigray People's Liberation Front (TPLF) that prompted the suspension of commercial flights last month. The TPLF has been fighting against pro-government forces since September 23, raising fears of an all-out civil war similar to that of 2020-2022.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopian army pushes back Tigrayan rebels</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2778e3247a4ab8b6b4e296e96fb58a0f9176b274de3e7869343c569f0117f5bf</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T20:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261002-ethiopian-army-pushes-back-tigrayan-rebels--c1af64eb04a0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261002-ethiopian-army-pushes-back-tigrayan-rebels" /><summary type="html">Ethiopia and Eritrea have severed ties and with tensions spreading across the region, the African Union is urging all sides to show restraint. Meanwhile, Ethiopia's army is advancing toward the Tigrayan capital as fighting intensifies and new explosions rock Addis Ababa.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>On the run for 20 years, Ugandan warlord Kony still 'active' within the Lord's Resistance Army</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dc988266a79cafb04958478dca7e37b51c22b4b6e966f23d79818315685ab679</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T19:31:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261002-on-the-run-for-20-years-ugandan-warlord-kony-still-active-within-the-lord-s-resistance-army--aeeee67f194b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261002-on-the-run-for-20-years-ugandan-warlord-kony-still-active-within-the-lord-s-resistance-army" /><summary type="html">In recent months, the eastern Central African Republic has been hit by several attacks attributed to the Lord’s Resistance Army (LRA), a Ugandan militia infamous for its massacres and mass abductions of children in the 1990s and 2000s. The group's leader, Joseph Kony, wanted by the International Criminal Court for more than 20 years, remains at large. FRANCE 24 spoke to Leonie von Braun, the ICC’s lead investigator on the Kony case, about the group's resurgence.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia and Eritrea break diplomatic ties over conflict</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fb8d6e748054cefc1e97da115c300e055b70526b679546bce320082b32e383ef</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T20:28:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ethiopia-and-eritrea-break-diplomatic-ties-over-conflict--12a4e73260b2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ethiopia-and-eritrea-break-diplomatic-ties-over-conflict" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition: Ethiopia and Eritrea break diplomatic ties, accusing each other of stoking internal conflicts. Also, Nigeria rolls out a digital postcode system for every building. Plus we speak to one of the co-founders of the Rural Women's Assembly as it is recognised for its work challenging power systems.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopian AI expert, Timnit Gebru, wins 'alternative Nobel'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5c44c748d249790090529d2cedc0c997f4f9143cd0a99b2dd2acdabc969185f0</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T20:44:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ethiopian-ai-expert-timnit-gebru-wins-alternative-nobel--fc9f29a4fc4c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ethiopian-ai-expert-timnit-gebru-wins-alternative-nobel" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition: Africa's richest man breaks ground on a $16 billion oil refinery in Kenya. Also, at universities across Cameroon, programming is overshadowed with uncertainty amidst an indefinite strike by lecturers. Plus we speak to Ethiopian-born computer scientist and pioneering AI ethicist Timnit Gebru as she is honoured with the Swedish Right Livelihood Award for her work on how AI is influenced by biases.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia back to civil war? Horn of Africa fears spillover effect of renewed fighting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2a31c5217dd9c6c803bdb023b09d6fbd917fbe5258282ce7ec65a8c6094ef3d9</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T19:04:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260930-ethiopia-back-to-civil-war-horn-of-africa-fears-spillover-effect-of-renewed-fighting--2f65ee3843c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260930-ethiopia-back-to-civil-war-horn-of-africa-fears-spillover-effect-of-renewed-fighting" /><summary type="html">After contagion in the Arabian Peninsula, should the entire Horn of Africa fear a domino effect? Just as US President Donald Trump’s decision to invade Iran drew the Saudis back to Yemen, did threats over the Bab al-Mandab Strait light the fuse in Ethiopia, where last week, unresolved issues between the government and its Tigray region erupted? Could a potential return to civil war draw in regional rivals?</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia's last Jews dream of visa for Israel</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:85a9515402ad375bdee824a501683a5062fc84afbd5d020aea82536053340dc7</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T09:55:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260930-ethiopia-s-last-jews-dream-of-visa-for-israel--0983188429c0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260930-ethiopia-s-last-jews-dream-of-visa-for-israel" /><summary type="html">Ethiopia has one of the oldest Jewish communities in the world, rumoured to be the descendants of the Queen of Sheba and King Solomon in 950 BC. From the 1970s to 1990s, this community known as Beta Israel was persecuted under the Communist regime, and Israel evacuated more than 20,000 Ethiopian Jews in dramatic airlifts known as Operation Solomon and Operation Moses. But a few thousand were left behind.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Ugandan coronation comes under social media scrutiny</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e4eb318c5c30d142ab502c24ce667e1fdd95bec337bc99fcbd5e217d87f82c6a</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T20:22:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ugandan-coronation-under-social-media-scrutiny--bc49397c37a1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ugandan-coronation-under-social-media-scrutiny" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition: Uganda's new king of Tooro is crowned before thousands of people. Also, Africa's richest man cautions the continent against losing control of its major projects. And dozens of civilians are killed as Ethiopian government forces bombard towns in the northern region of Tigray.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Morocco's king appoints Marrakesh mayor El Mansouri as first woman prime minister</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2793718bfaa1c80d028892eb7b0b5c33daab60bb263c0ef77811e80d597d7625</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T16:08:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20260929-morocco-king-appoints-first-woman-prime-minister-el-mansouri-after-parliamentary-vote--45f176d87012.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260929-morocco-king-appoints-first-woman-prime-minister-el-mansouri-after-parliamentary-vote" /><summary type="html">King Mohammed VI appointed Fatima Ezzahra El Mansouri as Morocco's first woman prime minister on Tuesday after her liberal-centrist party came out on top in a September 23 parliamentary election, the royal palace said. Her government is expected to make major investments linked to the 2030 FIFA World Cup, while facing pressing issues including unemployment and living costs.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Ebola a 'terrifying disease': Conflict-ravaged DRC faces overburdened healthcare system</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:828cb19e983997f77f7411514804a4d27a73b20fe7d1f3f419601ce765302414</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T10:09:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260929-ebola-a-terrifying-disease-as-drc-faces-decades-of-conflict-and-overburdened-healthcare-sys--656d2bdf0d4d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260929-ebola-a-terrifying-disease-as-drc-faces-decades-of-conflict-and-overburdened-healthcare-system-1" /><summary type="html">Eve Irvine is pleased to welcome Stephanie Hoffmann, Project Coordinator for Butembo, North Kivu, Doctors Without Borders. The Ebola outbreak is hitting a region already ravaged by decades of armed conflict, insecurity, and an overwhelmed health system. As the epidemic's epicenter shifts from Ituri to North Kivu, the disease is spreading and the transmission is accelerating. In Butembo, a densely populated city of around 2 million, health workers themselves are being placed in an impossible position, often caring for their neighbors and relatives without adequate protective equipment.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ethiopian forces claim to have retaken key Tigray town</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dc82ab0fd1cdf5dc0ccfdd35129e037d951fb7d52976c4a0305e760a06573c65</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T20:32:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ethiopian-forces-claim-tigray-town--a7d829132c01.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ethiopian-forces-claim-tigray-town" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition: Ethiopia's army says it's seized a key city in the northern region of Tigray amidst escalating conflict with local rebels. Also, two mass shootings in South Africa leave at least 28 dead. Plus Ugandan activist Praise Aloikin Opoloje is facing court after she turned up following days of uncertainty about her whereabouts.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Trump granting asylum to Afrikaners is 'race-based policy', South African FM claims</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c62eadeb638ea773a9c73f4ca893b9f1eee83708b0ef652f5207c771545028b8</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T10:38:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t_te-_-t_te/20260928-trump-granting-asylum-to-afrikaners-is-race-based-policy-south-african-fm-claims--ce5df4a22d5f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20260928-trump-granting-asylum-to-afrikaners-is-race-based-policy-south-african-fm-claims" /><summary type="html">In an interview with FRANCE 24 on the sidelines of the UN General Assembly in New York, South African Foreign Minister Ronald Lamola said Washington's plan to take in up to 17,500 more White South Africans was "a race-based policy", dismissing the "so-called genocide" of Afrikaners as "fake news".</summary><category term="Tête à tête" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia accuses Eritrea, Sudan of backing Tigray rebels amid clashes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:637c00a9f0aa60ae3bb32dbb9a8cfb275ca0c7c679fa5b4111f4d7d3151ba85a</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T23:27:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20260927-ethiopia-accuses-eritrea-sudan-backing-tigray-rebels--b54da5cdf6a1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260927-ethiopia-accuses-eritrea-sudan-backing-tigray-rebels" /><summary type="html">Ethiopia’s army chief accused Eritrea and Sudan on Sunday of backing armed groups fighting federal troops, as clashes with Tigrayan rebels intensified. The Tigray People’s Liberation Front said it was waging a “defensive war” and seized airports. A humanitarian source said rebels captured the Afar town of Erebti on Sunday.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>South Africa shootings leave 27 killed</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c70f2e21cffc0e1645585746e1869aa98c96f3db4f3c04c81aba5e1535559253</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T13:56:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/south-africa-shootings-leave-27-killed--c505b1841bd3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/south-africa-shootings-leave-27-killed" /><summary type="html">It has been a deadly night in South Africa, with 27 people killed in two separate shooting incidents. Police say 17 people were shot dead at a tavern outside Johannesburg by suspects armed with assault rifles, while another 10 were killed near Cape Town when gunmen opened fire at a venue selling grilled meat. No arrests have been made as police search for the attackers. Initial investigations suggest one shooting may have been linked to a turf war between illegal miners, while the other could have stemmed from a business rivalry. France 24 correspondent Eurice Masson reports the latest from South Africa.</summary></entry><entry><title>Femicides on the rise in South Africa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c9e8fec906cee417deb654b3a2531d29c3e56556592834ac2190eb025d0c2008</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T13:51:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/femicides-on-the-rise-in-south-africa--439af0aa2c75.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/femicides-on-the-rise-in-south-africa" /><summary type="html">Two more women have been found dead in Johannesburg this weekend, bringing the number of women killed in a single municipality to 11 in just two months. Most of the other victims were in their 20s and 30s, with some found partially undressed and showing signs of sexual assault, raising fears that a serial killer could be responsible. Police have offered a $25,000 reward for information leading to the arrest of the suspected killer or killers. The deaths have sparked a national outcry over violence against women in South Africa, which has one of the world’s highest rates of gender-based violence. Tegan Snayman, Research, Campaigns and Communications Assistant at Amnesty International South Africa, shares further insights.</summary></entry><entry><title>Gunmen kill at least 27 people in separate mass shootings in South Africa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d5517ff1bb9905b9d499e568b2ad897f194a0e7ac08b2987967c958a20bc9bcc</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T12:34:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20260927-gunmen-kill-27-people-in-separate-mass-shootings-in-south-africa--48f7dc4b3928.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260927-gunmen-kill-27-people-in-separate-mass-shootings-in-south-africa" /><summary type="html">At least 27 people were killed in separate mass shootings in Cape Town and Johannesburg, police said Sunday. No suspects have been arrested in either shooting, and the motives for the attacks remain unknown.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>‘Super El Niño’ deepens hunger crisis in South Sudan says UN</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:06a216a608ebae244d90a4d5f6eb6fbbb71a2a35299ded83683a678c2a5a0ac6</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T10:06:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260926-super-el-ni_o-deepens-hunger-crisis-in-south-sudan-says-un--c820ea8f62e0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260926-super-el-ni%C3%B1o-deepens-hunger-crisis-in-south-sudan-says-un" /><summary type="html">"The already dire hunger crisis in South Sudan is becoming increasingly critical as violence, extreme weather and dwindling aid leave millions without enough food" says UN.</summary></entry><entry><title>Morocco’s Authenticity and Modernity Party wins parliamentary election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4a3fba345af0e6e1936d2ee15d5e6f3b1cbbd167d952cd0311ea32a3449e3045</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T09:38:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/morocco-s-authenticity-and-modernity-party-wins-parliamentary-election--1daba84b0262.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/morocco-s-authenticity-and-modernity-party-wins-parliamentary-election" /><summary type="html">Morocco’s Authenticity and Modernity Party won the most seats in the country’s parliamentary election, taking 97 of 395 seats in the House of Representatives, according to final results announced by the Interior Ministry on Friday. The party, founded by a royal adviser close to King Mohammed VI and known by its French acronym PAM, fell short of an absolute majority and will need to negotiate with other parties to form a governing coalition.</summary></entry><entry><title>Heavy fighting on multiple fronts between Ethiopian forces and rebel groups</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6ca3c6fd3a7bb20920fa6dfcb2a54ef7e8657a1dd8cb779ebdf8782a204409a7</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T09:26:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/heavy-fighting-on-multiple-fronts-between-ethiopian-forces-and-rebel-groups--e78db56fc270.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/heavy-fighting-on-multiple-fronts-between-ethiopian-forces-and-rebel-groups" /><summary type="html">Fighting appears to be worsening in Ethiopia after the TPLF said it was in a "full blown" blown war with federal forces this week, days after the Tigrayan rebels declared a coalition with six other armed groups across the country, all with the objective of overthrowing prime minister abiy ahmed's government. And as of friday, it appears that another armed group has claimed to have joined the alliance. More from our correspondent in Addis Ababa Tom Canetti.</summary></entry><entry><title>Telecoms disruption raises fears as heavy fighting strikes Ethiopia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:04f334d351da28057a469ae0b35823f9495197350c400413e4570b0711a0b195</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T20:32:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20260925-telecoms-disruption-raises-fears-as-heavy-fighting-strikes-ethiopia--7d5d81c48ccb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20260925-telecoms-disruption-raises-fears-as-heavy-fighting-strikes-ethiopia" /><summary type="html">First, fighting continues between Ethiopian forces and the Tigray People's Liberation Front as fears of a regional spillover continue to mount. Next, in DR Congo, both the opposition and the ruling UDPS party continue to blame each other for the violence at a mass protest 10 days ago. Plus the Authenticity and Modernity Party looks to form a coalition in Morocco to address top voter issues, including the cost-of-living crisis.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Each side feels it 'could get a decisive military victory' in Sudan, Trump's Africa envoy says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:62f98e5d02a43ad69b7f104fe21a60f205f56e3e4362b86e7a938ac05da2f055</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T12:54:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t_te-_-t_te/20260925-each-side-feels-it-could-get-a-decisive-military-victory-in-sudan-trump-s-africa-envoy-says--9207dc16119d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20260925-each-side-feels-it-could-get-a-decisive-military-victory-in-sudan-trump-s-africa-envoy-says" /><summary type="html">In an interview with FRANCE 24 on the sidelines of the UN General Assembly, Trump's Africa envoy Massad Boulos said that each side in Sudan feels it "could get a decisive military victory". Asked about Western Sahara, he acknowledged there is no "imminent solution that we can feel or touch". He also rejected Rwanda's accusations of bias over US sanctions, saying they "can easily be reversed".</summary><category term="Tête à tête" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia: what's driving the renewed violence in Tigray?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:243ae525985c414c6342002d05f00706e5a3e9249bd2c5d76d7ea6539bb2eed3</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T11:15:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ethiopia-what-s-driving-the-renewed-violence-in-tigray--2c6abb0159c4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ethiopia-what-s-driving-the-renewed-violence-in-tigray" /><summary type="html">Tigray's rebel authorities say they are now in a "full-blown war" with the Ethiopian government, as fighting spreads into the neighbouring Amhara and Afar regions. Ethiopia's federal army says 272 rebels were killed and 260 wounded in the north, while FRANCE 24 spoke to Jervin Naidoo, Political Analyst at Oxford Economics Africa, to assess the seriousness of the escalation and explain what is driving the renewed violence in northern Ethiopia</summary></entry><entry><title>Senegal: power cuts return as Dakar swelters in the heat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d41fb577f5bbdac4d70369d93677b6ce73ba42734e6df0c93c7be12f653e0d0d</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T11:14:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/senegal-power-cuts-return-as-dakar-swelters-in-the-heat--fd18df6442db.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/senegal-power-cuts-return-as-dakar-swelters-in-the-heat" /><summary type="html">After years of largely stabilising its electricity supply, Senegal is once again facing power cuts, with outages returning to Dakar in September. The blackouts are fuelling frustration among residents as the capital endures a spell of intense heat.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia: Tigray rebels claim "full-blown war"</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f24cb2520013bf1afd15dce94dd1a6bdecdb8a1d2659f74b8b9ab82a474e4fe8</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T11:13:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ethiopia-tigray-rebels-claim-full-blown-war--9b074c24592a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ethiopia-tigray-rebels-claim-full-blown-war" /><summary type="html">The Tigray People's Liberation Front says it is in a "full-blown war" with Ethiopia's federal government after seizing key airports and launching attacks into the neighbouring Amhara and Afar regions. The escalation comes days after the TPLF joined six other armed groups in a new alliance against the government, raising fears of a return to the devastating 2020-2022 conflict that killed at least 600,000 people.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia: renewed Tigray fighting raises fears of return to civil war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3ee388ce9bca3ea082cdab2e4acf254a8ec33e87083e7aa690a8cb61eb70e55f</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T11:12:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ethiopia-renewed-tigray-fighting-raises-fears-of-return-to-civil-war--a8794692057f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ethiopia-renewed-tigray-fighting-raises-fears-of-return-to-civil-war" /><summary type="html">Fears are mounting that Ethiopia could be sliding back towards civil war as fighting intensifies in the north, with the army saying it killed 272 TPLF fighters in Amhara while the rebels describe the conflict as a "full-blown war." The escalation comes after the TPLF joined a new alliance with six other armed groups. FRANCE 24's Tom Canetti has the latest from the ground.</summary></entry></feed>
